  summary: Cauliflower is a kind of cabbage! Its white head, called the curd, is
    made of flowers that haven't opened yet.
  facts:
  - Cauliflower isn't only white. It can be orange, purple, green or brown too!
  - "Cauliflower likes cool weather, around 60\xB0F, to grow its head."
  - If cauliflower gets too dry, it only grows small heads.
  sources:
  - Encyclopaedia Britannica. Cauliflower. https://www.britannica.com/plant/cauliflower
  - University of Minnesota Extension. Crop and field planning tools for vegetable
    farmers. https://extension.umn.edu/agriculture/specialty-crops/vegetable-farming/crop-and-field-planning-tools-for-vegetable-farmers
  realGrowTime: about 75 to 80 days after planting outside
  realHarvestPattern: Before harvest, farmers tie the big leaves over the head to
    shade it!
